  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> We know that sum of equidistant term from end &amp; beginning is same in any <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo></math><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>114</mn></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>114</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>38</mn></math></p><p>Then,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>11</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>16</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>16</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>76</mn></math></p>",
